1
00:00:01,170 --> 00:00:01,820
Ohhh!

2
00:00:02,540 --> 00:00:04,220
Meet oa and ow.

3
00:00:05,020 --> 00:00:08,050
Two spellings, one long O sound.

4
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:09,500
You hear it in boat.

5
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:10,850
And in snow.

6
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,400
Same sound, different spelling.

7
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:16,420
So which one do we write?

8
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:18,880
Ask the same question.

9
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:21,060
WHERE is the sound?

10
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:25,190
At the beginning, in the middle, or at the end?

11
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:28,920
In the MIDDLE, we write oa.

12
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:29,900
B.

13
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:29,980
Oa.

14
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:31,400
T.

15
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:33,180
Boat!

16
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:35,960
Letters on both sides of it.

17
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:38,910
At the END, we write ow.

18
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:40,900
Sn.

19
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:42,260
Ow.

20
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:43,740
Snow!

21
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:45,660
Nothing after it.

22
00:00:46,140 --> 00:00:46,880
So we use ow.

23
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:49,960
We never write bowt.

24
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:52,340
And we never write snoa.

25
00:00:54,740 --> 00:00:55,620
Oa in the middle.

26
00:00:56,420 --> 00:00:57,740
Ow at the end.

27
00:00:58,500 --> 00:00:59,120
Let's see it.

28
00:00:59,880 --> 00:00:59,960
Boat.

29
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:01,820
Coat.

30
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:03,300
Goat.

31
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:05,020
Road.

32
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:06,520
Toast.

33
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:08,100
Soap.

34
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:11,560
All oa, all in the middle.

35
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:13,280
Now the end.

36
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:14,780
Snow.

37
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:16,520
Grow.

38
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:18,200
Blow.

39
00:01:19,380 --> 00:01:20,080
Slow.

40
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:22,080
Show.

41
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:23,940
Yellow.

42
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:27,200
All ow, all at the end.

43
00:01:28,140 --> 00:01:28,760
Your turn!

44
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:30,270
Here's the word.

45
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:31,960
Road.

46
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:33,980
Is it oa, or ow?

47
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:34,880
It's oa!

48
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:37,360
The sound is in the middle.

49
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:38,780
So remember.

50
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:43,940
Oa sails in the middle, ow rolls to the end.

51
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:47,920
Read more words like these in the English Learning app.

52
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:49,750
Free to download today!
